From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0946 redfin: CPU present past the GPU ring, ticks on the INTF
 frame counter, present latency in the stats

The present blit was queued ~50 us after SwapEnd but landed 23-28 ms later,
behind backboardd's next frame on the single ring. sweetfbx & 8 (off by
default): the present thread scales the frame onto the panel itself (GPU
path geometry, nearest sample, corner mattes), after a clean+invalidate of
the source; with sweetfbflip=1 into the back buffer and flipped. 0944's
tick phasing falls back to INTF1's frame counter (0x0ac) when the tear
check's counter reads 0: edges found by 20 us polling at the first tick and
every 32 ticks. The stats line gets "| vis V us cpu C us": mean SwapEnd ->
panel-visible (blit landed or CPU copy done) and mean CPU copy time.
While bit 0x8 is on the present thread is bound to CPU6 (sweetfbcpu=N).
Poke "p fbx HEX" sets bits 0x2/0x4/0x8 live ("SWEET FB: fbx now 0x..").
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_gpu.c                   |  67 +++++++
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp | 333 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 392 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_gpu.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_gpu.c
index c439593..c998d97 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_gpu.c
